NOTE = '''0.4.21 (2026-10-30) = THE RARITY + TOOLTIP PASS (Skyy 2026-10-24: "make that the global default. if it has a rarity, it gets color coded.
  if it has flavor text, the text is well laid out, well organized, clear, readable, and color coded." + 2026-10-18 "color code everything").
  LOOKS ONLY: no saved data, no config row, no lang key name, no behaviour changed; the layout copies the approved Pets tooltip (PetsPage.tip).
  1. Hatchery egg grid tooltip (PetHatchery.eggCell): the egg name in its rarity colour + dim "x<n>"; dim "In your Void: " + gold count
     (only with eggs in the Void); HATCHES (soft white "Hatches in " + gold time); PETS (soft white odds / the dragon line); RARITY ODDS;
     the yellow / grey click footer exactly as before.
  2. Hatchery Fuse pets grid tooltip (PetHatchery.petCell): the type line (kept); "<Rarity> <Kind>" in the rarity colour + gold
     "x<n> owned"; FUSING ("Fusing: " soft white + the state green when it can fuse, dim when not); dim "Mythic pets come only from eggs.";
     the footer as before.
  3. Egg item flavor text (lang items.<egg>.description / server.items.<egg>.description, the 30 eggs + our 4 dragon / secret eggs): the
     SAME words, the tier tag first in the egg's rarity colour, then a line break (lang \\n, LangFileParser turns it into a new line), the
     sentence soft white, the craft / trade note dim, "Rare to Mythic" in their own colours. With the spans stripped and the \\n put back
     to " - " each text equals 0.4.20's byte for byte (asserted at build time).
  4. Hatch page titles: #SkyyHtName (the held egg's name) and #SkyyHtResN (the result "Rare Wolf") in the rarity colour - the same
     runtime TextColor route as the page's status line (skyyui label col=J(...), the colorOf(this.info) pattern shipped since 0.4.0).
  SAVED DATA: none. FLOOR (rollback): rolls back alone to 0.4.20 (looks only). The 0.4.20 / 0.4.19 / 0.4.17 / 0.4.15 / 0.4.11 floors stand.
'''

P = G.Patch(os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyPets", "build_skyypets_0.4.20.py"), os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyPets", "build_skyypets_0.4.21.py"))
